#. Tag: title
#: intro.docbook:6
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: intro.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kexi; is a database management application. It can be used for creating "
"databases, inserting data, performing queries, and processing data. Forms "
"can be created to provide a custom interface to your data. All database "
"objects - tables, queries and forms - are stored in the database, making it "
"easy to share data and design."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: intro.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kexi; is part of the &koffice; productivity suite for the K Desktop "
"Environment."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: intro.docbook:26
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In addition to storing your &kexi; databases in files, &kexi; can also store "
"your data on a <firstterm>database server</firstterm>. Using a database "
"server allows you to share your database with other people, and also allows "
"more than one person to use the database at one time. The following database "
"servers are supported by &kexi;:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: intro.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"MySQL (See <ulink url=\"http://www.mysql.com/\">http://www.mysql.com/</"
"ulink>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: intro.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"PostgreSQL (See <ulink url=\"http://www.postgresql.org/\">http://www."
"postgresql.org/</ulink>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: intro.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"More information about &kexi; can be found at the &kexi; page on the "
"&koffice; website at <ulink url=\"http://www.koffice.org/kexi/\">http://www."
"koffice.org/kexi/</ulink>, and on the website for &kexi; itself at <ulink "
"url=\"http://www.kexi-project.org/about.html\">http://www.kexi-project.org/"
"about.html</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: intro.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have any questions about &kexi;, there are two mailing lists you can "
"use. The <ulink url=\"mailto:kexi@kde.org\">Kexi user mailing list</ulink> "
"can be used to ask questions about using &kexi; or about the &kexi; project. "
"The <ulink url=\"mailto:kexi-devel@kde.org\">Kexi development mailing list</"
"ulink> can be used to ask questions about the development of &kexi;. Further "
"information on how to subscribe to these lists, together with a few other "
"ways of making contact with &kexi; developers, can be found at:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: intro.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid "http://www.kexi-project.org/support.html"
msgstr ""

